    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d463">

                <pb facs="0751" n="615" xml:id="pg615"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.79611 Tri-Motors Safety Airways/22:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Uruguay</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gade</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-05-13T11:00:00-03:30">May 13, 1929—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:38 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>27. Department’s 8, April 30, 2 p.m.<anchor n="59" xml:id="d463-f1"/> I have been
                    unofficially informed that permission for flights will be granted by the
                    Ministry of War. Ministry of Finance has not yet replied but is expected to
                    accord free entry.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gade</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
